WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.760
East London.

2
00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.910
Mayes Brook once ran through
a park in a concrete channel,

3
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.630
fenced off and largely invisible.

4
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:13.690
Between March 2011 and October 2012,
1.6 kilometres of brook were brought out

5
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.350
of that channel into the park.

6
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.870
Workers created 1.5 hectares
of new floodplain storage,

7
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.730
and planted 3 hectares of woodland.

8
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:27.650
The aim: a showcase of how green space
can help a community cope with the risks

9
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.470
from climate change.

10
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.670
So did setting the brook loose
make the area safer, and greener?

11
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.190
In this mission, you'll meet the agencies,

12
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.510
charities, insurer and
neighbours involved.

13
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.170
Then you'll test each
aim against the evidence,

14
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:43.790
one by one.

15
00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:49.320
Your mission: evaluate whether freeing
Mayes Brook made the area safer and greener.
